  "label": "User projected onto the hateful text message",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'go be gay somewhere else' because the meme uses this phrase as a direct, confrontational address to the viewer, implying that the viewer (or their identity) is being told to leave or be excluded from the depicted scene. The text functions as a deictic statement directed at the user, making them the target of the exclusionary message. The visual of riot police and violence serves as the context for this projection, reinforcing the hostile environment the text implies the user should abandon.",
